      "announcement": "Engineer TEST Development — Empfehlungsbund.de Firmenfinder Jobsuche EB-Talents FAQ DE EN Für Arbeitgeber Startseite Firmenverzeichnis GlobalFoundries Management Services GmbH & Co. KG Engineer TEST Development Engineer TEST Development GlobalFoundries Management Services GmbH & Co. KG Dresden Engineer TEST Development GlobalFoundries Management Services GmbH & Co. KG Dresden Bewerben About GF GlobalFoundries® Inc. (GF®) is one of the world's leading semiconductor manufacturers. GF redefines innovation and semiconductor manufacturing by developing and delivering feature-rich process technology solutions with leading performance in all growth markets. GF offers a unique mix of design, development and manufacturing services. With a talented and diverse team and manufacturing locations in the U.S., Europe and Asia, GF is a trusted technology provider to its global customers. GF employs approximately 13,000 people, including more than 3,000 in Dresden, Germany. For more information, visit hier . Introduction GlobalFoundries operates a Test Facility at the Dresden site. As part of the fab, Test is responsible for the functional testing of the manufactured wafers, known as wafer sorting. The development of test solutions for autonomous mobility, Industry 4.0 and 5G in Europe is an interesting and great challenge for which we would like to expand the team with an experienced Test Development Engineer. Your Job As a Test Engineer you will be responsible for the development of test programs and test hardware for the functional test of SOC devices with memory, NVM, logic and mixed signal as well as RF components and the transfer of the test programs into production. The work task includes: Development of test concepts, test hardware and test programs for the functional test of devices with memory, NVM, logic and mixed signal/RF components Electrical characterization of NVM, memory logic and mixed signal/RF devices to support our technology development, yield engineering and quality teams Installation, correlation and release of test programs and test hardware for production Yield optimization, test time reduction and continuous improvement of the test process Creation of test project documentation Required Qualifications Completed Master's Degree or Diploma in the fields of information technology/communications engineering/electrical engineering/physics or comparable Professional experience in electrical test beneficial Very good knowledge of electronic measurement methods Programming skills in C/C++/Java/Python Knowledge in test hardware design (schematics, probe hardware preparation) is an advantage Knowledge in memory test procedures is an advantage Very good written and spoken English skills We Offer The position is open-ended and to be filled as soon as possible. Attractive compensation components: 13th month salary, bonus payments, assistance with relocation to Dresden. Flexible working time arrangements: Family friendly part-time models, trust flextime, salary conversion into free time Diverse opportunities for further development: Career stages for every job, internal qualification offers, promotion of external educational qualifications Focus on your health: On-site gym and beach volleyball court, bike leasing, subsidized employee restaurant Corporate culture: Cooperation at eye level - everyone is on first name terms with us, budget for individual team events, social commitment via GlobalGives You can find more benefits in detail at hier Diversity is part of our corporate DNA. For this reason, we would like to encourage women in particular to apply for a job with us. As we value equal opportunities and inclusion is particularly important to us, we welcome applications from people with disabilities. This job posting is for a position up to pay group ENG 2 GlobalFoundries Compensation CBA. Information about our benefits you can find here: hier CHIP Englisch Herr Maik Rohne, Sr Specialist Talent Acquisition